    "name": "Seabed Settlers",
    "steam_appid": 2984470,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Seabed Settlers</strong> is a city-building strategy game set beneath the waves of a ruined Earth,  inspired by classics such as Ceasar III, Anno, Pharaoh and others. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Humanity has fled the surface, now rendered uninhabitable by radiation. You are the Overseer of one of the last hopes for civilization\u2014tasked with building, sustaining, and expanding a self-sufficient underwater colony. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2984470/extras/67b1b16a7b65be713869f1bec616e941.avif?t=1752603827\" width=600 height=224 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A City Beneath the Sea</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a city-building strategy game set beneath the waves of a ruined Earth. Humanity has fled the surface, now rendered uninhabitable by radiation. You are the Overseer of one of the last hopes for civilization\u2014tasked with building, sustaining, and expanding a self-sufficient underwater colony.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Deep Systems, Classic Roots</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Seabed Settlers draws inspiration from classic city-builders of the late 90s and early 2000s\u2014games that emphasized long-term planning, resource balance, and interconnected systems. Structures evolve as needs are met. Immigration flows based on reputation and stability. A poorly managed city may spiral out of control\u2014just as success can snowball into expansion and new opportunities.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2984470/extras/d6c1153e9f006f52b9f494e62bed1c03.avif?t=1752603827\" width=600 height=224 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Don't Grow Too Fast</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With the right know-how you can pass the earlier levels relatively quickly. Soon however you will find that you need to carefully manage the amount of habitats compared the amount of resources and infrastructure. The key to success is gradual and planned improvement of your city.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Threats From the Deep</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Survival isn\u2019t just about food and shelter. Radiation-born mutants now roam the oceans, and failing to maintain proper defenses can have dire consequences. Some maps demand careful placement of sentries, resource prioritization, and emergency response systems. From pirate raids to searing heat and internal strife\u2014every threat needs a solution.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2984470/extras/b3d9463d64ec4e20e974748504feb1bf.avif?t=1752603827\" width=600 height=224 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A Growing Challenge</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game features a handcrafted campaign with multiple scenarios. Each new zone brings unique terrain, resources, and environmental challenges. You'll unlock new technologies and structures as you progress\u2014upgrading your colony\u2019s capabilities while expanding your influence across the seabed.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Designed for Strategy Fans New and Old</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Seabed Settlers aims to capture the spirit of the classics while offering quality-of-life improvements and modern presentation. Whether you\u2019ve spent hundreds of hours in old-school city-builders or are discovering the genre for the first time, the game provides a structured but flexible experience.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your choices shape the survival\u2014and potential rebirth\u2014of humanity. No two colonies will be the same.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Seabed Settlers</strong> is a city-building strategy game set beneath the waves of a ruined Earth,  inspired by classics such as Ceasar III, Anno, Pharaoh and others. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Humanity has fled the surface, now rendered uninhabitable by radiation. You are the Overseer of one of the last hopes for civilization\u2014tasked with building, sustaining, and expanding a self-sufficient underwater colony. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2984470/extras/67b1b16a7b65be713869f1bec616e941.avif?t=1752603827\" width=600 height=224 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A City Beneath the Sea</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a city-building strategy game set beneath the waves of a ruined Earth. Humanity has fled the surface, now rendered uninhabitable by radiation. You are the Overseer of one of the last hopes for civilization\u2014tasked with building, sustaining, and expanding a self-sufficient underwater colony.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Deep Systems, Classic Roots</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Seabed Settlers draws inspiration from classic city-builders of the late 90s and early 2000s\u2014games that emphasized long-term planning, resource balance, and interconnected systems. Structures evolve as needs are met. Immigration flows based on reputation and stability. A poorly managed city may spiral out of control\u2014just as success can snowball into expansion and new opportunities.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2984470/extras/d6c1153e9f006f52b9f494e62bed1c03.avif?t=1752603827\" width=600 height=224 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Don't Grow Too Fast</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With the right know-how you can pass the earlier levels relatively quickly. Soon however you will find that you need to carefully manage the amount of habitats compared the amount of resources and infrastructure. The key to success is gradual and planned improvement of your city.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Threats From the Deep</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Survival isn\u2019t just about food and shelter. Radiation-born mutants now roam the oceans, and failing to maintain proper defenses can have dire consequences. Some maps demand careful placement of sentries, resource prioritization, and emergency response systems. From pirate raids to searing heat and internal strife\u2014every threat needs a solution.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2984470/extras/b3d9463d64ec4e20e974748504feb1bf.avif?t=1752603827\" width=600 height=224 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A Growing Challenge</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game features a handcrafted campaign with multiple scenarios. Each new zone brings unique terrain, resources, and environmental challenges. You'll unlock new technologies and structures as you progress\u2014upgrading your colony\u2019s capabilities while expanding your influence across the seabed.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Designed for Strategy Fans New and Old</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Seabed Settlers aims to capture the spirit of the classics while offering quality-of-life improvements and modern presentation. Whether you\u2019ve spent hundreds of hours in old-school city-builders or are discovering the genre for the first time, the game provides a structured but flexible experience.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your choices shape the survival\u2014and potential rebirth\u2014of humanity. No two colonies will be the same.</p>",
    "short_description": "A city-builder inspired by classics like Caesar III, Anno, and Pharaoh\u2014set on the ocean floor. Build, manage, and expand your underwater colony as humanity flees a dying world. Balance resources, population, and survival in this deep colony sim across a structured campaign.",
